{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>By the lash of a tongue</b> — For the evil tongue is like a lash. And more accurate: that it is the tongue of a nation, as in: לשונות הגוים (tongues of the nations)." "<b>And lash</b> — From: שוטטו בחוצות ירושלם (they roam the streets of Jerusalem) (Lamentations 4:14); as a tongue roams, so you will hide in your land."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:54.308864872Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}